<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      App Group entitlement for the Control daemon
      (docs/proposals/desktop-macos-integration.md §2.1).

      Grants access to the shared group container
      ~/Library/Group Containers/<TEAMID>.app.tenshu.shared/ where the daemon
      binds its IPC + native-bridge sockets, so the sandboxed Drive File
      Provider extension can reach them. @TEAM_ID@ is substituted by the
      :control-desktop:signControlAppForAppGroup Gradle task.

      Note: we deliberately do NOT enable com.apple.security.app-sandbox here —
      the JVM daemon needs broad host access; the app-groups entitlement still
      grants the shared container. The File Provider .appex (Phase 2) is the
      sandboxed peer and carries its own entitlements.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>@TEAM_ID@.app.tenshu.shared</string>
    </array>

    <!--
      ⚠⚠ Load-bearing for LAUNCH, not for permissions.

      signControlAppForAppGroup signs with `--options runtime` (hardened runtime),
      which turns on **Library Validation** — and that refuses to load a dylib whose
      Team ID differs from the main executable's. This is a jpackage app: the bundled
      JDK's `libjli.dylib` keeps its own (Adoptium) team, so a hardened-runtime signing
      without this key produces an app that fails at launch with
      `dlopen ... different Team IDs`.

      Harmless here because this bundle is deliberately NOT sandboxed (see above) — it
      is a JVM host that already has broad host access.

      The ordinary local install path (`signDesktopApp`,
      gradle/desktop-app-signing.gradle.kts) sidesteps the whole problem by not using
      hardened runtime at all; this key is what keeps the entitlement-carrying,
      notarisation-oriented path launchable.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
